cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this dataset, please cite it as below. Code is MIT-licensed; the
  derived data layers are CC-BY-4.0 (see LICENSE and DATA-LICENSE.md — the
  underlying Utah public records are not subject to this project's copyright).
title: "civic-data: Utah government records, from city councils to the State"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Welsh
    given-names: Tyson
repository-code: "https://github.com/tysonwelsh/civic-data"
url: "https://municipalsky.com"
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: "2026-07-31"
date-released: "2026-07-31"
abstract: >-
  A structured, quantifiable archive of Utah government records built for
  housing, growth, and development research: 44 registered entities in a
  4-tier model (31 cities/towns, 8 counties, 2 metropolitan planning
  organizations, and the State of Utah), federated into one queryable SQLite
  database with extracted roll-call votes, public comments, election results,
  campaign finance, adopted ordinances, programmed regional projects,
  population projections, rolling council rosters, and a full-text search
  layer — with per-record provenance and measurement ceilings carried as
  queryable caveats. Coverage and known limitations are documented per entity;
  honest gaps are reported, never filled.
keywords:
  - Utah
  - municipal government
  - city council
  - roll-call votes
  - land use
  - housing policy
  - elections
  - campaign finance
  - civic data
